 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Farewell, my dear boy! When haply again\nWe meet thee on that fatiguing journey,\nWhen first I saw thy face and echoes\nOf thy kindly voice from those green valleys,\nMay thou forget my love. And when again,\nWho sees the outline of my vanquished heart,\nAnd finds a new friend in one who believes\nIn pity - whom shall not thus repent? Love,\nI have no wish to forgive; but alone\nMy soul does think of thee. Farewell, dear.\nBEAUDE LA TRANCHE (1806), La Vie de M. Pierre.\nHeart of mine, whose heart was made to forever",
